# gov_epoch_budget_v1.tau  --  ZenoDEX governance: AGGREGATE movement-budget bit (per revision)
# MUTABILITY: UPDATABLE (the gate logic; the budget is supplied per call)
# SHAPE: factored partial sums. The per-surface gates bound each surface's step and the
# drift-budget bit bounds each surface's window trajectory -- but a multi-surface action
# can still move EVERY surface one legal step at once (a coordinated regime walk). This
# bit bounds the AGGREGATE: the total |delta| of one applied revision across all touched
# surfaces, grouped exactly as the loop gates them (scalars / router shares / collateral
# pair), must fit the aggregate budget.
#
# The three group sums are computed by the RUNTIME from the validated delta map (the
# Python mirror recomputes them itself from the raw deltas -- stricter, never weaker);
# the spec validates the budget relation including its no-wrap guards. Same honest
# boundary as `curr` (WS2): the spec bounds the relation, the runtime owns the inputs.
#
# Inputs:
#   i1 = scalar_sum     (bv[16]) -- |dfee| + |dfunding_cap| + |dredeem_staker|
#   i2 = router_sum     (bv[16]) -- |dbuyburn| + |dstakers| + |dreserve| + |dhosts|
#   i3 = collateral_sum (bv[16]) -- |dmcr| + |dccr|
#   i4 = budget         (bv[16]) -- aggregate movement budget for one revision
# Output:
#   o1 = within_budget (sbf) -- 1 iff the (non-wrapping) total <= budget
#
# Wrap-safety: bv[16] addition is MODULAR; `a + b >= a` is the standard unsigned
# no-overflow guard, chained across both additions, so a wrapped "small" total can
# never be admitted.

always
  (o1[t]:sbf = 1:sbf <->
    ( ((i1[t]:bv[16] + i2[t]:bv[16]) >= i1[t]:bv[16])
      && (((i1[t]:bv[16] + i2[t]:bv[16]) + i3[t]:bv[16]) >= (i1[t]:bv[16] + i2[t]:bv[16]))
      && (((i1[t]:bv[16] + i2[t]:bv[16]) + i3[t]:bv[16]) <= i4[t]:bv[16])
    )
  ).
